examples.solution_text:
(a) The boundaries are one standard deviation below and above the mean.
$P(60<X<68)\approx0.68$.
(b) The interval runs from the mean to two standard deviations above it. Symmetry gives half of the central $95\%$ band.
$\begin{aligned}&\mathrel{\phantom{=}}P(64<X<72)\\&\approx0.95\div2\\&=0.475\end{aligned}$
The shaded region shows part (b).
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.85cm,y=1cm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{bandfill}{HTML}{D4E8FF}
\fill[bandfill] (0,0) -- plot[domain=0:2,samples=50,variable=\x] ({\x},{1.8*exp(-\x*\x/2)}) -- (2,0) -- cycle;
\draw[black,thick] plot[domain=-3.8:3.8,samples=100,variable=\x] ({\x},{1.8*exp(-\x*\x/2)});
\draw[black,->] (-4,0)--(4,0);
\foreach \a/\b in {-1/60,0/64,1/68,2/72}{\draw[black] (\a,0)--(\a,-0.1) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\b$};}
\draw[black,dashed] (0,0)--(0,1.8);
\draw[black,dashed] (2,0)--(2,{1.8*exp(-2)});
\path (0.8,0.6) node {$47.5\%$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

$100=90+2(5)$, so the boundary is two standard deviations above the mean. The two tails share the area outside the central $95\%$ band equally.
$\begin{aligned}&\mathrel{\phantom{=}}P(X>100)\\&\approx(1-0.95)\div2\\&=0.025\end{aligned}$
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.85cm,y=1cm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{bandfill}{HTML}{D4E8FF}
\fill[bandfill] (2,0) -- plot[domain=2:3.8,samples=50,variable=\x] ({\x},{1.8*exp(-\x*\x/2)}) -- (3.8,0) -- cycle;
\draw[black,thick] plot[domain=-3.8:3.8,samples=100,variable=\x] ({\x},{1.8*exp(-\x*\x/2)});
\draw[black,->] (-4,0)--(4,0);
\foreach \a/\b in {-2/80,0/90,2/100}{\draw[black] (\a,0)--(\a,-0.1) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\b$};}
\draw[black,dashed] (2,0)--(2,{1.8*exp(-2)});
\path (2.8,0.8) node {$2.5\%$};
\draw[black] (2.8,0.6)--(2.5,0.06);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

$28=26+2$, so the boundary is one standard deviation above the mean. Add the half below the mean to half of the central $68\%$ band.
$\begin{aligned}&\mathrel{\phantom{=}}P(X<28)\\&\approx0.5+0.68\div2\\&=0.84\end{aligned}$
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.85cm,y=1cm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{bandfill}{HTML}{D4E8FF}
\fill[bandfill] (-3.8,0) -- plot[domain=-3.8:1,samples=80,variable=\x] ({\x},{1.8*exp(-\x*\x/2)}) -- (1,0) -- cycle;
\draw[black,thick] plot[domain=-3.8:3.8,samples=100,variable=\x] ({\x},{1.8*exp(-\x*\x/2)});
\draw[black,->] (-4,0)--(4,0);
\foreach \a/\b in {0/26,1/28}{\draw[black] (\a,0)--(\a,-0.1) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\b$};}
\draw[black,dashed] (0,0)--(0,1.8);
\draw[black,dashed] (1,0)--(1,{1.8*exp(-0.5)});
\path (-0.9,0.6) node {$50\%$};
\path (0.5,0.6) node {$34\%$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

$210=200+10$ and $220=200+2(10)$. Subtract the mean-to-one-standard-deviation area from the mean-to-two-standard-deviation area.
$\begin{aligned}&\mathrel{\phantom{=}}P(210<X<220)\\&\approx0.95\div2-0.68\div2\\&=0.475-0.34\\&=0.135\end{aligned}$
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.85cm,y=1cm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{bandfill}{HTML}{D4E8FF}
\fill[bandfill] (1,0) -- plot[domain=1:2,samples=50,variable=\x] ({\x},{1.8*exp(-\x*\x/2)}) -- (2,0) -- cycle;
\draw[black,thick] plot[domain=-3.8:3.8,samples=100,variable=\x] ({\x},{1.8*exp(-\x*\x/2)});
\draw[black,->] (-4,0)--(4,0);
\foreach \a/\b in {0/200,1/210,2/220}{\draw[black] (\a,0)--(\a,-0.1) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\b$};}
\draw[black,dashed] (1,0)--(1,{1.8*exp(-0.5)});
\draw[black,dashed] (2,0)--(2,{1.8*exp(-2)});
\path (2.6,1.2) node {$13.5\%$};
\draw[black] (2.3,1.05)--(1.5,0.3);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

$30=40-2(5)$ and $45=40+5$. The interval crosses the mean, so add the areas on its two sides.
$\begin{aligned}&\mathrel{\phantom{=}}P(30<X<45)\\&\approx0.95\div2+0.68\div2\\&=0.475+0.34\\&=0.815\end{aligned}$
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.85cm,y=1cm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{bandfill}{HTML}{D4E8FF}
\fill[bandfill] (-2,0) -- plot[domain=-2:1,samples=70,variable=\x] ({\x},{1.8*exp(-\x*\x/2)}) -- (1,0) -- cycle;
\draw[black,thick] plot[domain=-3.8:3.8,samples=100,variable=\x] ({\x},{1.8*exp(-\x*\x/2)});
\draw[black,->] (-4,0)--(4,0);
\foreach \a/\b in {-2/30,0/40,1/45}{\draw[black] (\a,0)--(\a,-0.1) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\b$};}
\draw[black,dashed] (-2,0)--(-2,{1.8*exp(-2)});
\draw[black,dashed] (0,0)--(0,1.8);
\draw[black,dashed] (1,0)--(1,{1.8*exp(-0.5)});
\path (-0.9,0.6) node {$47.5\%$};
\path (0.5,0.6) node {$34\%$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

$780=900-2(60)$ and $960=900+60$.
$\begin{aligned}&\mathrel{\phantom{=}}P(780<X<960)\\&\approx0.475+0.34\\&=0.815\end{aligned}$
Multiply the estimated probability by the number of components.
$\begin{aligned}f&=np\\&\approx2500\times0.815\\&=2037.5\end{aligned}$
About $2038$ components are expected to last within the interval.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.85cm,y=1cm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{bandfill}{HTML}{D4E8FF}
\fill[bandfill] (-2,0) -- plot[domain=-2:1,samples=70,variable=\x] ({\x},{1.8*exp(-\x*\x/2)}) -- (1,0) -- cycle;
\draw[black,thick] plot[domain=-3.8:3.8,samples=100,variable=\x] ({\x},{1.8*exp(-\x*\x/2)});
\draw[black,->] (-4,0)--(4,0);
\foreach \a/\b in {-2/780,0/900,1/960}{\draw[black] (\a,0)--(\a,-0.1) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\b$};}
\draw[black,dashed] (-2,0)--(-2,{1.8*exp(-2)});
\draw[black,dashed] (0,0)--(0,1.8);
\draw[black,dashed] (1,0)--(1,{1.8*exp(-0.5)});
\path (-0.5,0.6) node {$81.5\%$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

$338=320+3(6)$, so this volume is three standard deviations above the mean.
$\begin{aligned}&\mathrel{\phantom{=}}P(X>338)\\&\approx(1-0.997)\div2\\&=0.0015\end{aligned}$
Only about $0.15\%$ of drinks contain $338$ mL or more, so this volume is unusual.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.85cm,y=1cm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{bandfill}{HTML}{D4E8FF}
\fill[bandfill] (3,0) -- plot[domain=3:3.8,samples=50,variable=\x] ({\x},{1.8*exp(-\x*\x/2)}) -- (3.8,0) -- cycle;
\draw[black,thick] plot[domain=-3.8:3.8,samples=100,variable=\x] ({\x},{1.8*exp(-\x*\x/2)});
\draw[black,->] (-4,0)--(4,0);
\foreach \a/\b in {0/320,3/338}{\draw[black] (\a,0)--(\a,-0.1) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\b$};}
\draw[black,dashed] (3,0)--(3,{1.8*exp(-4.5)});
\path (2.7,0.9) node {$0.15\%$};
\draw[black] (2.9,0.7)--(3.3,0.01);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
